00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:52,280
I'll be reworking it a bit.

248
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:58,500
Really, you saw yesterday.

249
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:01,420
I think it can give more kilowatts.

250
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:04,580
I'm going out today, I'll buy some normal diodes.

251
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:08,760
And I'll pull this thing out.

252
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:09,980
There they are, the diodes are sitting there.

253
00:16:10,780 --> 00:16:14,420
And I'll move these diodes here.

254
00:16:15,060 --> 00:16:16,920
I'll put a big heatsink here.

255
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:19,060
Or I'll put a fan.

256
00:16:19,160 --> 00:16:22,020
Maybe even this fan in a sandal here.

257
00:16:22,180 --> 00:16:26,220
So I open the plugs here so the air comes out from here.

258
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:29,820
And then I'll be able to put in stronger diodes.

259
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:35,000
And plug in a load not just 4 kilowatts of something.

260
00:16:35,180 --> 00:16:40,440
But something bigger maybe.

261
00:16:40,860 --> 00:16:45,900
It seems to me I was surprised yesterday that there wasn't even a sag.

262
00:16:46,140 --> 00:16:48,980
When I was stuffing the plug in there.

263
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:54,020
More precisely, not the plug, but these wires for another two kilowatts.

264
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:57,720
I mean easily, and it didn't twitch at all there.

265
00:16:58,780 --> 00:17:03,440
But that says you can probably stuff in a bit more of something.

266
00:17:04,020 --> 00:17:04,580
We'll see.

267
00:17:04,660 --> 00:17:13,240
It's just that if the voltage drops below 160 volts, my self-feeding power supply turns off and that's it — it's not enough for it.

268
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:18,400
I had this trouble where there were 167 volts and it worked.

269
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:24,080
As soon as I loaded it more there, it shut off, didn't want to work.

270
00:17:24,860 --> 00:17:28,320
The result was good, but a bit too little.

271
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:32,740
You have to bring the voltage up to 200, at least 220 volts, at least 216.

272
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:36,620
In the field yesterday somehow this didn't work out for me.

273
00:17:36,740 --> 00:17:38,780
I haven't figured it out yet.

274
00:17:38,980 --> 00:17:39,540
But that's okay.

275
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:45,500
These are already the little things in life compared to what's already worked, what results we already have.

276
00:17:46,260 --> 00:17:49,820
So, I say once again — here at the end there has to be a good support.

277
00:17:49,920 --> 00:18:01,240
If there's no good support, everything you have, as soon as the push comes here, will be all here in the wire, and you don't get anything, no power.

278
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:02,740
But this affects the power.

279
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:11,340
So, on this coil here, I say once again, it's wound simply, nothing complicated.

280
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:16,820
You can just wind a simple coil under this and take from it, but you'll affect it inductively.

281
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:23,420
So a removable bifilar gets wound, which doesn't inductively affect this coil.

282
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:23,960
That's it.

283
00:18:24,040 --> 00:18:28,020
I mean it does affect, but its influence isn't as high as this.

284
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:33,280
It takes off the energy, but at that they don't strongly affect each other.

285
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:46,540
Also, what I wanted to say — so here at mine, this comes from there, from the end, this is the pickup coil, and this coil here, it goes at the bottom.

286
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:47,740
This is the second coil.

287
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:52,980
These two ends here, they have to be on ground.

288
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:55,280
Strictly on ground, mandatory.

289
00:18:55,940 --> 00:19:00,460
Solder them straight onto this very terminal block.

290
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:04,040
So, well, something like this.

291
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:06,540
It's pointless to tell many of you.

292
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:10,020
I mean anyway you'll be looking for a catch.

293
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:12,740
Even if I put this device on Mars.

294
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:19,340
Turn it on — you'd say I took a phase from the aliens, because it's just trouble.

295
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:22,040
Nothing to be done.

296
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:28,260
You're used to combustion, so to speak, carbon combustion and so on?

297
00:19:28,780 --> 00:19:31,180
What you've been taught and what you have to pay for?

298
00:19:32,220 --> 00:19:35,300
There — Tesla rightly said that it should be free.

299
00:19:35,620 --> 00:19:39,740
Basically, around us there's a huge amount of energy, everything is spinning everywhere.

300
00:19:40,980 --> 00:19:46,220
I think there's some kind of sense in thinking about this.

301
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:46,760
Okay.
